import json, os, sys
HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)); PE = os.path.dirname(HERE); sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(PE, 'python'))
from pe import tie_policy as tp
J = lambda p: json.load(open(os.path.join(PE, 'reports', p)))
P = J('r1_tie_order/r1_tie_order_sensitivity.json'); I = J('m2f_audit/r1/independent_tie_sensitivity_result.json'); S = J('m2f_audit/r1/sensex_tid_investigation_result.json'); N = J('m2f_audit/r1/nifty_id_evidence_result.json')
pol = P['policies']; ORDER = ['sells_first', 'buys_first', 'trade_id', 'order_no', 'sensex_trade_id_time']; n = lambda x: f'{x:,}'
L = ['# R1 — Intra-second fill-order convention: policy, evidence and consequences', '',
     '**Status: APPROVED by the project owner (Option A).** Generated by `tools/r1_report.py` from the committed result files; every number below traces to `reports/r1_tie_order/` (production pipeline) or `reports/m2f_audit/r1/` (independent references that import no `pe` code).', '',
     '## 1. The convention', '',
     f"**`{tp.SOURCE_ROW_ORDER_CONVENTION}`** is the primary deterministic convention of the whole historical reconstruction (lineage, closing batches, wing/body, forensics, figures, case studies): fills of the same instrument that share one second are processed in **source-file row order**. It is a deterministic convention, **not verified intra-second execution chronology**. Source timestamps have one-second resolution; no raw column carries sub-second time except the SENSEX trade id (section 4). Previously delivered numerical outputs are unchanged by this work (verified byte-for-byte against the baseline taken before any R1 change).", '',
     '## 2. Policies', '', '| Policy | Role | Key | Where implemented |', '|---|---|---|---|']
for nme, p in tp.POLICIES.items(): L.append(f"| `{nme}` | {'**PRIMARY**' if p.primary else 'sensitivity-only'} | {p.description} | {'Python and C++ (parity-tested)' if p.cpp_supported else 'Python only'} |")
L += ['', 'A sensitivity policy never replaces the primary convention: the delivered-output builders assert `require_primary`, every `LineageSet` carries `convention` (`SOURCE_ROW_ORDER_CONVENTION` or `SENSITIVITY_ONLY:<policy>`), and the convention identifier is stamped into the four delivered manifests and every run manifest. The legacy token `src` is the same convention (the engine dump still says `src`, so delivered bytes are unchanged).', '',
      '## 3. What changes under each alternative (full ledger, production pipeline vs source-row order)', '',
      'The five populations below are **different things and must not be conflated**.', '',
      '### 3.1 Population 1: groups whose ORDER differs', '', f"Same-instrument, same-second groups with at least two fills: **{n(pol['trade_id']['1_groups_differing_in_order']['multi_fill_groups'])}**.", '', '| Policy | Groups whose order differs | of which mixed-side | of which same-side |', '|---|---:|---:|---:|']
for k in ORDER: g = pol[k]['1_groups_differing_in_order']; L.append(f"| `{k}` | {g['differing']} | {g['differing_mixed_side']} | {g['differing_same_side']} |")
L += ['', 'A differing order is **not** an accounting effect: most such groups contain only same-side fills far from any position flip.', '', '### 3.2 Population 2: groups that change the OPENING / CLOSING allocation', '', 'A group matters only when inventory crosses zero inside the second. This happens in **same-side** groups too, not only in mixed-side groups.', '',
      '| Policy | Groups | mixed-side | same-side | Fills whose open/close split changes | Exact source rows (0-based) |', '|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|']
for k in ORDER: g = pol[k]['2_groups_changing_open_close_allocation']; L.append(f"| `{k}` | {g['groups']} | {g['mixed_side']} | {g['same_side']} | {g['fills_changed']} | {', '.join(map(str, g['fill_rows'])) or '-'} |")
L += ['', '| Policy | Changing groups: instrument, second, source rows, sides |', '|---|---|']
for k in ORDER:
    for d in pol[k]['2_groups_changing_open_close_allocation']['groups_detail']: L.append(f"| `{k}` | {d['instrument']} @ {d['ts']}: rows {d['rows']} sides {d['sides']} |")
L += ['', '### 3.3 Population 3: episodes and instruments whose identity changes', '', '| Policy | Episodes changed | Instruments changed | Instruments | Reversal-ended episodes (primary -> alternative) |', '|---|---:|---:|---|---|']
for k in ORDER: e = pol[k]['3_episode_identity']; L.append(f"| `{k}` | {e['episodes_changed']} | {e['instruments_changed']} | {', '.join(e['instruments']) or '-'} | {e['reversal_episodes_base']} -> {e['reversal_episodes_alt']} |")
L += ['', '### 3.4 Population 4: closing-batch membership (C1 and C2 are identical in every row)', '', '| Policy | Batches not in the alternative @2/5/10/30/60 s (baseline 7,127 / 3,777 / 3,065 / 2,171 / 1,502) | Parents in the changed batches @10 s / @60 s |', '|---|---|---|']
for k in ORDER:
    b = pol[k]['4_closing_batch_membership']; L.append(f"| `{k}` | " + ' / '.join(str(b[f'C1@{t}s']['baseline_batches_not_in_alternative']) for t in (2, 5, 10, 30, 60)) + f" | {b['C1@10s']['parents_in_changed_batches']} / {b['C1@60s']['parents_in_changed_batches']} |")
L += ['', '### 3.5 Population 5: wing/body membership', '', f"Baseline links: " + ', '.join(f"{m} {n(v)}" for m, v in pol['trade_id']['5_wing_body_membership']['links_baseline'].items()) + '.', '', '| Policy | Items only in one | W1 | W1_S60 | W2 | W2_S60 | W3 links changed | Opening body units | Closing body units |', '|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
L.append(f"| `source_row` (baseline) | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 626,765 | 540,250 |")
for k in ORDER: w = pol[k]['5_wing_body_membership']; lc = w['links_changed']; L.append(f"| `{k}` | {w['items_only_in_one']} | {lc['W1']} | {lc['W1_S60']} | {lc['W2']} | {lc['W2_S60']} | {lc['W3']} | {n(w['opening_body_units'])} | {n(w['closing_body_units'])} |")
L += ['', '### 3.6 Invariants (every policy)', '', '| Policy | Opening units | Closing units | Final inventory per instrument |', '|---|---:|---:|---|']
for k in ORDER: v = pol[k]['invariants']; L.append(f"| `{k}` | {n(v['opening_units'])} ({'equal' if v['opening_units_equal'] else 'DIFFERS'}) | {n(v['closing_units'])} ({'equal' if v['closing_units_equal'] else 'DIFFERS'}) | {'equal' if v['final_inventory_equal'] else 'DIFFERS'} |")
L += ['', 'Cash flow is also invariant, and the realized P&L deltas for these policies are 0 (exact arithmetic, independent reference). Attribution of batch / wing-body changes to the changed-split groups is by shared parent order id and is an upper bound on direct causation (`attribution` in the JSON).', '',
      '### 3.7 Stress orders (independent reference; NOT plausible chronologies)', '', 'Reversed source order and five fixed-seed random within-second permutations (seeds 11-15) show how large the sensitivity can get. They are stress tests, never candidate truths.', '',
      '| Order | Instruments | Episodes | Fills with changed split | Reversal fills | FIFO realized delta (paise) | LIFO realized delta (paise) | Batches not in alternative @10 s | W1 / W1_S60 links changed |', '|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|']
for k in ['reversed_src'] + [f'random_seed{s}' for s in (11, 12, 13, 14, 15)]:
    a = I[k]['accounting']['FIFO']; b = I[k]['accounting']['LIFO']; L.append(f"| {k} | {a['instruments_changed']} | {a['episodes_identity_changed']} | {a['fills_open_close_split_changed']} | {a['reversal_fills']} | {a['realized_delta_paise']:.0f} | {b['realized_delta_paise']:.0f} | {I[k]['batches']['C1@10s']['baseline_batches_not_in_alternative']} | {I[k]['wing_body']['links_changed']['W1']} / {I[k]['wing_body']['links_changed']['W1_S60']} |")
e1 = S['1_format']; e2 = S['2_relation_to_epoch']; e5 = S['5_ordering']; e4 = S['4_duplicates_collisions']; e6 = S['6_semantics']; e7 = S['7_effect']
L += ['', '## 4. SENSEX trade-id timestamp: separate validation (sensitivity-only)', '',
      f"* **Extraction rule.** All {n(e1['sensex_fills'])} SENSEX trade ids match `^<19 digits>-<1..9 digits>$` ({n(e1['match_19digit_dash_suffix'])}); the 19-digit prefix is a nanosecond epoch timestamp. NIFTY trade ids are plain integers with no dash: **different semantics, never assumed to carry time.**",
      f"* **Relation to the raw epoch column.** `epoch == round-half-up(ns/1e9)` for {n(e2['epoch_equals_round_half_up'])} of {n(e1['sensex_fills'])} fills ({n(e2['epoch_equals_floor'])} where the fraction is below .5, {n(e2['epoch_equals_ceil'])} where it is at least .5); ns minus epoch lies in about -500..+500 ms (p01 {e6['ns_minus_epoch_ms_quantiles']['p01']} ms, median {e6['ns_minus_epoch_ms_quantiles']['p50']} ms, p99 {e6['ns_minus_epoch_ms_quantiles']['p99']} ms).",
      f"* **The exceptional fill.** Row {S['3_exceptional_fills'][0]['row']} (`{S['3_exceptional_fills'][0]['inst']}`, parent {S['3_exceptional_fills'][0]['parent']}, sell {S['3_exceptional_fills'][0]['qty']}): its id time is {S['3_exceptional_fills'][0]['diff_s']:.1f} s AFTER its epoch. The policy never trusts an id whose rounded time differs from the epoch: it falls back to the epoch-derived time for that fill.",
      f"* **Duplicates and collisions.** {e4['duplicate_full_trade_ids']} duplicate full trade ids; {e4['duplicate_ns_prefixes_global']} duplicate nanosecond prefixes overall, {e4['same_ns_prefix_in_same_instrument_second_group']} inside same-instrument-second groups (several fills from one matching event; their relative order is not decidable from the id and falls back to source-row order).",
      f"* **Ordering consistency.** {n(e5['multi_fill_groups'])} same-instrument-second groups with >=2 fills; the nanosecond order differs from file order in {e5['file_order_differs_from_ns_order']} (all same-side; {e5['mixed_side_that_differ']} of {e5['mixed_side_groups']} mixed-side groups; no group shares a parent). Across instruments within a second the file is not ns-sorted ({n(S['5b_global_within_second']['file_order_ns_nondecreasing'])} of {n(S['5b_global_within_second']['adjacent_same_second_pairs'])} adjacent pairs non-decreasing), which is why the policy compares only within an instrument.",
      f"* **Semantics.** Of {e6['parents_with_multiple_fills']} multi-fill parents, ns is non-decreasing in file order in {e6['parents_ns_increasing_in_file_order']}: consistent with per-fill match/report time, not order-placement time. It is **not proven** to be execution chronology.",
      f"* **Effect.** Applying it to SENSEX (NIFTY stays source-row) changes **nothing**: {e7['accounting']['FIFO']['fills_open_close_split_changed']} fills, {e7['accounting']['FIFO']['episodes_identity_changed']} episodes, 0 batches, 0 wing/body links.",
      '* **Conclusion.** The evidence supports a SENSEX-only **sensitivity** policy (`sensex_trade_id_time`). It is not the primary convention: nothing in the data proves the embedded time is the exchange execution order, and the effect on every result is nil.', '',
      '## 5. NIFTY trade id and order number: not chronology', '',
      f"* NIFTY trade ids are not time-monotone: {n(N['nifty_trade_id_vs_time_per_IST_day']['fills_with_key_below_max_of_earlier_seconds'])} of {n(N['nifty_trade_id_vs_time_per_IST_day']['fills_compared'])} later-second fills have an id below the maximum id of earlier seconds in the same IST day ({n(N['nifty_trade_id_vs_time_per_instrument']['fills_with_key_below_max_of_earlier_seconds'])} of {n(N['nifty_trade_id_vs_time_per_instrument']['fills_compared'])} within one instrument).",
      f"* Order numbers are not time-monotone either: NIFTY {n(N['nifty_order_number_vs_time_per_IST_day']['fills_with_key_below_max_of_earlier_seconds'])} of {n(N['nifty_order_number_vs_time_per_IST_day']['fills_compared'])}; SENSEX {n(N['sensex_order_number_vs_time_per_IST_day']['fills_with_key_below_max_of_earlier_seconds'])} of {n(N['sensex_order_number_vs_time_per_IST_day']['fills_compared'])}.",
      f"* NIFTY same-instrument-second groups with >=2 fills: {n(N['nifty_multi_fill_groups']['groups'])}; file order differs from trade-id order in {N['nifty_multi_fill_groups']['file_order_differs_from_trade_id_order']}.",
      f"* Mixed-side groups (all instruments): {N['mixed_side_groups_all_instruments']['groups']}; trade-id order differs from file order in {N['mixed_side_groups_all_instruments']['trade_id_order_differs_from_file']}, order-number order in {N['mixed_side_groups_all_instruments']['order_number_differs_from_file']}.",
      f"* Columns scanned for sub-second values: none ({len(N['columns_with_time_like_values'])} time-like columns, all minute resolution).", '',
      '## 6. Correction of the earlier audit statement', '',
      'The M2-F report said trade id contradicts file order in "only two mixed-side groups". That is **true but incomplete** as an explanation of accounting sensitivity: those two groups (rows 726-728 and 9688-9689) do not change any opening/closing allocation. The accounting-relevant disagreements are **two same-side groups at a position flip** (CE24600 rows 27911 / 27917 and PE23200 rows 27912 / 27916 on 2026-09-01), where trade id and order number agree with each other against file order. Population 1 (order differs), 2 (allocation changes), 3 (episode identity), 4 (batches) and 5 (wing/body) above are reported separately for that reason. Amendments to D-A01, B-01 and C-01: `reports/m2f_audit/r1/amendments.json`.', '',
      '## 7. What must not be concluded', '',
      '* Episode identities, reversal counts, opening/closing allocation membership, FIFO/LIFO attribution, closing-batch membership and wing/body membership are **not order-independent facts**; they are conditional on `SOURCE_ROW_ORDER_CONVENTION`.', '* Aggregate opening/closing units, final inventory per instrument and cash are invariant under every tested order.', '* No alternative order is claimed to be the historical truth.', '* The true intra-second order of NIFTY fills is not recoverable from the source.', '',
      '## 8. Delivered outputs affected by the convention (values unchanged; listed so users know what is conditional)', '',
      'M2-B lineage (episode identity, reversal count, OA/CP membership, FIFO/LIFO CA); M2-C closing batches (all 10 views); M2-D items and links (W1, W1_S60, W2, W2_S60, W3); M2-E datasets, V1-V6, case studies and records. Metadata change: `tie_order_convention` added to four manifests (`reports/m2f_audit/r1/affected_files_plan.md`); no data value changed.']
open(os.path.join(PE, 'reports', 'R1_TIE_ORDER_CONVENTION.md'), 'w').write('\n'.join(L) + '\n'); print(len(L), 'lines')
